The **Property** module gives a note fields of its own: tags, a due date, a rating, a checkbox. They live in a **Property** block, and the block is optional: a note needs none. Back to [[Welcome]].

Property:
	Tag: [Guide, Module]
	Module: Property
	Rating: 5
	Reviewed: True
	Due: 2026-10-05
	Exam: 2026-10-12 09:00 -04:00

- Add one with **+ Add property** under the name, with `/property` where you are writing, or with `Ctrl+;`.
- It is a block like any other, so it can sit anywhere: drag its ⋮⋮ handle to move it, even into a callout or a column. Tags and search find it wherever it is.
- Each field has a type: Text, List, Number, Checkbox, Date, or Date & time. Click its icon to change the type, and drag the icon to move the field.
- Tags are pills: click one to edit it, drag it to move it, and press **+** to add one. `Enter` or a comma starts the next.
- The fields are plain `Key: value` lines in the basic types of YAML, so other tools can read them.

Callout {Kind: Info}: The note's own header stays out of the way
	`Created`, `Id`, and `Format` belong to the app. They show only in the Source view.
